.TH "GLESHA-CLEANUP" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-cleanup \- delete local archive copies that are stored remotely
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha cleanup\fR SET [options]
.br
\fBglesha cleanup\fR \-\-all [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete the archive copies kept in the local state of SET, or of every set with \-\-all, once a remote copy has been verified. Remote objects and archives outside the state directory are never touched.
.PP
Sets with pending or unresolved work are skipped. The files are listed and confirmed before deletion.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-all
Process every set.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
List the files without deleting them.
.TP
.B \-\-assume\-yes
Answer yes to all confirmations.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha cleanup docs \-\-dry\-run
glesha cleanup \-\-all \-\-assume\-yes
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-status (1)
